---
// A post page's header on the deep field, its picture in a white frame and its text (Feature 006
// #147; Feature 009 #285; spec #280 "Post page: the header", "Post page: the picture", "Post page:
// the text"). The `header` slot lies on the field (DeepField.astro), and the default slot is the
// text on the page's colour: an Activity's details card, or a News or Health Content post's body,
// source and topics (PostBody.astro). The text starts 32 px under the field below lg and 40 px from
// lg, or 32 px under the frame where the frame comes before it (Product Owner, 2026-11-14: #285
// comment 6877659654, item 2).
//
// The block is a grid of the page's column between two gutters, so the field spans the window
// while the header, the frame and the text keep to the column. The field is the first row's
// height, which its header sets: it reaches 40 px under the header below `sm` and 48 px from `sm`,
// and 80 px below lg where the frame follows.
//
// - **From lg a post with a picture reads in two columns** ("สองคอลัมน์"): the text column, 44 rem
//   at most, a 3 rem gap and the frame, 28 rem wide, at the column's right. The frame starts on the
//   field, 4.25 rem under its top, level with the header's row of pills, and spans both rows of the
//   grid, so it runs over the field's lower edge when it is the taller. It stays in view 1.5 rem
//   below the site's header while the text scrolls ("ลอยตาม (แนะนำ)") and stops where the two
//   columns end: a grid item's grid area is its containing block (CSS Grid Layout 1, "Placing Grid
//   Items"), which a sticky box never leaves (CSS Positioned Layout 3, sticky positioning). So what
//   a page puts after this block, such as an Activity's photos, comes below the frame and never
//   under it (the Product Owner's finding of 2026-11-04, spec #144). The second row is flexible
//   (CSS Grid Layout 1's track sizing): an item that spans a flexible track gives its size to that
//   track alone, so the first row stays the header's height and the frame's extra height goes to
//   the second, where the text starts right under the field. Without text the second row holds
//   only what the frame adds, so the block ends with whichever of the field and the frame ends
//   lower, with no empty row or gap after it (#198; #190 comment 6707205912, Empty Post page row
//   B). The frame follows only while the text is the longer, and one taller than the window shows
//   its lower part as the block ends. The Product Owner kept both limits (2026-11-04: #147 comment
//   6634124888).
// - **Below lg** the page reads in one column: the header on the field, the frame, 48 rem wide at
//   most, starting 48 px above the field's lower edge, then the text (#285 comment 6877659654,
//   item 1).
// - **A post without a picture** keeps one column.
//
// A default slot that renders nothing counts as none, so a post with no text ends with its field or
// its frame. `Astro.slots.has` tells only that a page passed the slot (astro 7.3.5
// dist/core/render/slots.js), so the block renders it once with `Astro.slots.render` and places
// that HTML.
//
// The frame is white with the `deep` shadow, radius 24 and 10 px of padding, and holds the picture
// whole, at its own aspect ratio with corners of radius 18, and "เปิดภาพขนาดเต็ม" under it at every
// width, as a phone needs it most (Product Owner, 2026-11-04: #147 comment 6634124888). The picture
// fills the frame's width in a box shaped by the size EmDash keeps with the image
// (docs/agents/emdash-1.1.0.md "Media" says how), so a dominant colour EmDash's Image paints behind
// it never shows beside it (#147 comment 6628040681; its blurhash placeholder does not show at all,
// same section). It loads at once with a high fetch priority, since it is in view when the page
// opens (emdash 1.1.0 src/components/EmDashImage.astro). The link opens the file as it was
// uploaded, which EmDash stores unchanged (src/astro/routes/api/media.ts), whatever rendition the
// picture shows (ADR 0003), so a citizen can read a One Page's small print (#144 user story 17). It
// is an onward link on this site, so it ends in chevron-right (ArrowLink.astro), and it keeps the
// page's focus ring, on the white frame.
//
// With motion allowed the frame rises in after the header's text, as the Featured card follows the
// hero's text on the Homepage (`hero-enter`, src/styles/global.css; spec #280 "Motion"); the text
// shows at once.
import { Image } from "emdash/ui";
import { availableMedia, mediaFileHref } from "../lib/media";
import type { ImageFieldValue } from "../lib/news";
import ArrowLink from "./ArrowLink.astro";
import DeepField from "./DeepField.astro";

interface Props {
	/** The post's picture, its featured image field's value. */
	image: ImageFieldValue | null | undefined;
}

/** The picture's width: the frame's column from lg, the reading width below it. */
const PICTURE_SIZES = "(min-width: 64rem) 28rem, (min-width: 48rem) 48rem, 100vw";

const image = await availableMedia(Astro.props.image, Astro.locals.emdash);
const fullSizeHref = image && mediaFileHref(image, Astro.locals.emdash);
const textHtml = await Astro.slots.render("default");
const showsText = Boolean(textHtml?.trim());
---

<div
	class:list={[
		"grid grid-cols-[minmax(var(--page-gutter),1fr)_minmax(0,var(--container-content))_minmax(var(--page-gutter),1fr)]",
		image && "lg:grid-rows-[auto_1fr]",
	]}
>
	<DeepField kind="post" class="col-span-full row-start-1">
		<div class:list={["page-container relative pt-6 pb-10 sm:pb-12", image && "max-lg:pb-20"]}>
			<div class:list={[image && "lg:mr-124"]}>
				<slot name="header" />
			</div>
		</div>
	</DeepField>
	{image && (
		<div
			data-testid="picture-frame"
			class="hero-enter relative col-start-2 -mt-12 max-w-3xl self-start rounded-24 bg-surface-base p-2.5 shadow-deep [--hero-enter-delay:0.25s] lg:sticky lg:top-[calc(var(--header-offset)+1.5rem)] lg:row-span-2 lg:row-start-1 lg:mt-17 lg:w-112 lg:max-w-none lg:justify-self-end"
		>
			<Image
				image={image}
				priority
				sizes={PICTURE_SIZES}
				class="h-auto w-full rounded-18 bg-surface-soft"
			/>
			{fullSizeHref && (
				<div class="px-2.5 pt-1.5">
					<ArrowLink href={fullSizeHref}>เปิดภาพขนาดเต็ม</ArrowLink>
				</div>
			)}
		</div>
	)}
	{showsText && (
		<div class:list={["col-start-2 pt-8 lg:pt-10", image && "lg:row-start-2 lg:mr-124"]}>
			<Fragment set:html={textHtml} />
		</div>
	)}
</div>
